{"id":185789779,"slug":"the-frontier-star-ledger-winning","title":"The Frontier Star-Ledger: Winning Domain Rating by Writing This Very Newsletter.","subtitle":"The Frontier Psychiatrists, much to my suprise, is a legit news source according to the internet.","post_date":"2026-01-26T01:19:18.111Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/the-frontier-star-ledger-winning","wordcount":550,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:45:09.440Z","body_sha256":"c7aa81c290fec0ef3540bdc12ca4c59ea60a7ed647fbe32cf6114597ce384c3e","text_words":553,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>With great domain rating comes great responsibility.  I'm pretty sure that's what they said in Spider-Man.  And, after all, Peter Parker was a journalist.  Maybe that's the great power they were talking about?</p><p>Newspapers had distribution. Television shows have Nielsen ratings.  With the Internet, lets us do something more detailed.  We've got not only the number of people who come to your website, but how authoritative other people think it is.</p><p>Domain Rating is a measure, created by Ahrefs, to measure the following:</p><blockquote><p>“Website authority” is an SEO concept that refers to the “strength” of a given domain.</p><p>Some people call this “domain authority,” which is not to be confused with the Domain Authority (DA) metric from Moz. When we talk about domain authority, we’re talking about a general SEO concept that’s synonymous with “website authority.”</p><p>Here at Ahrefs, we have a website authority metric of our own called Domain Rating. It runs on a scale from zero to a hundred. The higher a website’s Domain Rating (DR), the stronger and more authoritative it is.</p></blockquote><p>They lay out how they do the math to get to their domain rating for any given site:</p><blockquote><p>Domain Rating (DR) looks at the quantity and quality of external backlinks to a website.</p></blockquote><ol><li><p>Look at how many unique domains link to the target website;</p></li><li><p>Look at the “authority” of those linking domains;</p></li><li><p>Take into account how many unique domains each of those sites link to;</p></li><li><p>Apply some math and coding magic to calculate “raw” DR scores;</p></li><li><p>Plot these scores on a 100-point scale.</p></li></ol><blockquote><p>Domain Rating doesn’t take into account any other variables like link spam, traffic, domain age, etc.</p><p>Learn more about Domain Rating <a href=\"https://ahrefs.com/blog/domain-rating/\">here</a>.</p></blockquote><p>That hundred point scale is logarithmic.  That is to say, it's not equidistant between any two numbers, and it gets harder and harder to have your domain rating get higher and higher.  Naturally, I checked my own website, The Frontier Psychiatrists:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_1o3!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F584ad097-d512-47ca-a2c5-365e9b8ffb04_1452x672.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_1o3!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F584ad097-d512-47ca-a2c5-365e9b8ffb04_1452x672.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_1o3!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F584ad097-d512-47ca-a2c5-365e9b8ffb04_1452x672.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_1o3!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F584ad097-d512-47ca-a2c5-365e9b8ffb04_1452x672.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!_1o3!,w_14